From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: SlotVector: reserve(n), and a growth that fails leaves the table as it was (KEEPS THE STORE)

Store: KEEPS THE STORE. Only src/common/slot_vector.h changes. It is not among the translation id's
418 inputs (translation_inputs.txt of the VM's last build, id 7f9773909a21e3689fd7c18d27a3c10c: the
translator reaches no slot_vector.h; the SINGLE files' includes are not followed); the console
compiles a rewritten copy (<build>/recovery/common/slot_vector.h, headless/slot_vector_recovery.cmake),
not an input either.

Why: run1395 (13 Nov, T166, the load into the area past the field) ended in SlotVector<Image>::Reserve:
the texture cache's image table doubled 2048 -> 4096 slots, one 10,354,696 byte operator new[]
(2528 bytes a slot; disassembly of Reserve at 0x174fef1 in T166's llvm-pie.elf), on GPUBack, with
the pool's largest free piece at 1-2 MiB (its crash log 2010-2017).

What:
- reserve(n): grows the table now to the next power of two of n, in one allocation (0891 calls it at
  boot); capacity(). Unused without 0891's switch.
- Reserve allocates the new array, the bitset's and the free list's room before it moves a slot, so a
  failed allocation leaves the table as it was. The free list gets room for every slot, so erase()
  never allocates (it is noexcept). Upstream's noexcept stays here; the console's rewrite drops it
  (front commit, slot_vector_recovery.cmake). Same slots, same order, same growth as before.
- Cost: the free list holds 4 bytes a slot of room from the first growth on (16 KiB at 4096 slots).

Checked: a native test of the rewritten header (clang, ASan, macOS): 168 refused growths of a full
32-slot table, contents intact, a freed slot reused, reserve(4096) and 4000 more inserts. PS5-target
syntax check (t174a/check). Not checked: a build, the console.
---
diff --git a/src/common/slot_vector.h b/src/common/slot_vector.h
index 4a1837ce7e..b3884d1f26 100644
--- a/src/common/slot_vector.h
+++ b/src/common/slot_vector.h
@@ -165,6 +165,20 @@ public:
         return values_capacity - free_list.size();
     }
 
+    /// Slots the table holds without growing (it doubles when they are all taken).
+    [[nodiscard]] size_t capacity() const noexcept {
+        return values_capacity;
+    }
+
+    /// Grows the table now to at least `wanted` slots (the next power of two), in one allocation,
+    /// so it does not double later at a bad moment (an area load with the pool short: 0890,
+    /// EDEN_UP_RESERVE_TABLES). Nothing when it already holds that many.
+    void reserve(size_t wanted) {
+        if (wanted > values_capacity) {
+            Reserve(std::bit_ceil(wanted));
+        }
+    }
+
 private:
     struct NonTrivialDummy {
         NonTrivialDummy() noexcept {}
@@ -206,7 +220,18 @@ private:
     }
 
     void Reserve(size_t new_capacity) noexcept {
+        // Every allocation first, then the moves (0890): when one of them fails nothing has
+        // changed yet. The console's copy of this header lets the failure out
+        // (headless/slot_vector_recovery.cmake); upstream's noexcept ends the program as before.
+        // free_list gets room for every slot, so erase never allocates.
         Entry* const new_values = new Entry[new_capacity];
+        try {
+            stored_bitset.reserve((new_capacity + 63) / 64);
+            free_list.reserve(new_capacity);
+        } catch (...) {
+            delete[] new_values;
+            throw;
+        }
         size_t index = 0;
         for (u64 bits : stored_bitset) {
             for (size_t bit = 0; bits; ++bit, bits >>= 1) {
